-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code and prior work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository vendors and adapts components of AgentDojo
(https://github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo), used as the agent runtime, task
suites, and evaluation harness. AgentDojo is distributed under the MIT License;
its task suites and attack scaffolding under `src/` retain that origin.
See: Debenedetti et al., "AgentDojo: A Dynamic Environment to Evaluate Prompt
Injection Attacks and Defenses for LLM Agents," NeurIPS 2024 Datasets & Benchmarks.

The ODILE training objective adapts the representation-rerouting idea of
circuit-breaker training (Zou et al., "Improving Alignment and Robustness with
Circuit Breakers," 2024) and the contrastive representation-learning objective of
Simko et al. (2025) to the agentic tool-calling setting.

Base models referenced by the recipes (Llama-3.1/3.3, Qwen2.5, Qwen3) are
subject to their respective upstream model licenses.
